.TH SYS:SEED 1 "SPP CLI" "Version 1.0" "SPP Manual"
.SH NAME
sys:seed \- Executes all database seeders for a specified application.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php sys:seed
.I [app_name]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Discovers and executes all database seeders residing in src/{app}/seeders/. Supports both modern SPPSeeder classes (with entity synthesis and log output) and legacy seeders via parameter reflection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B [app_name]
(Optional) The target application name under src/ (defaults to 'default').
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
Scans filesystem at src/{app}/seeders/, loads seeder classes, establishes database context, runs seeder routines, and outputs summary logs.
